[] Does this imply that a patchlevel 10 is on it way or did I miss it ?

originally pl7 was the final 3.0 patch (released feb. 90).  however,
there were some significant bugs and dev team released pl8 (june 90)
followed shortly afterwards by pl9 (aug. 90), the final patch.  after
a year of listening carefully for bug reports there's the _real_
final 3.0 patch, pl10.  its release has not been announced but it
will be announced here when its ready.  there's no more 3.0 after
pl10!  dev team has been (as expected) hard at work on 3.1.

[] Can someone reveal what we can expect in 3.1 ?

a larger binary, no doubt (3.0 doubled the size of the former 2.3).
by the time 3.1 is released (far distant future) it should be
reasonable to expect:

improved interface/handling
smarter/new dungeon denizens
extended 3.0 features (i.e artifacts and special levels, etc.)
more internal code optimizations
more consistency amongst ports and more ports supported
more bugs ...

i'd like to know what's in store for 4.0.

